  "practice": [
    "Say ই three times with a short, relaxed ee/i sound: i, i, i.",
    "Read each vocabulary word aloud and listen for ই at the beginning or ি after a consonant.",
    "Practice the vowel sign: ক + ি = কি, দ + ি = দি, and ন + ি = নি.",
    "Remember that ি is written before its consonant but pronounced after it: কি is ki, not ik."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "ই is generally pronounced like ee/i, similar to the vowel in see but often shorter.",
    "When ই follows a consonant, it is represented by the ি vowel sign (ই-কার): ক + ি = কি.",
    "The ি sign is written to the left of the consonant it belongs to, but its sound follows that consonant.",
    "Keep ই distinct from the longer ঈ in spelling. In modern Bengali speech, ই and ঈ are often pronounced alike."
  ]
